WEBVTT

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.450
Gammon Sakanoue came to me in search of an Armlet

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.480
and has obtained new power.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.540
Wha--?!

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.700
That’s horrible!
Gammon obtained an Armlet of Orpheus?!

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.840
And now he knows.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:23.090
He has learned that in the future, there are two of me.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.280
One is Kaito Daimon.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.500
The other is...

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.350
There’s another...?

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.010
Who could it be?

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.070
The future is trapped in a flux.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:42.700
It is up to you to decide which way it will swing,
Phi-Brain children.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.990
Cheers to 100-Star Jin

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.780
Excluding Kaito, the remaining candidates
Orpheus selected are

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:30.680
Gammon, Freecell, Raetsel and you, Director Rook.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:33.590
You’ve asked multiple nations to assist in

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:38.000
watching the Republic of Amgine and restrict my movement.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.680
It’s easy for me to see such blatant maneuvers.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:48.430
I am only blind to Kaito Daimon.
He is the one exception.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:53.690
Cease your meaningless resistance
and awaken as a Phi-Brain,

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.540
Rook Banjo Crossfield.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:11.710
Including me, the people currently challenging
Orpheus’ Trial of Puzzles include...

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.620
Freecell, you solved the puzzle, didn’t you?

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.910
Can you keep going?

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:44.110
Yeah. Someone has to catch up to
Kaito and then surpass him!

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.020
Freecell!

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.830
The more candidates, the better!

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.260
And then there’s Raetsel!

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.770
What is she going to do?!

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:16.000
No matter how many times you have
challenged my Trial of Puzzles,

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.400
you have not awoken as a Phi-Brain.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:24.790
Yet Gammon Sakanoue’s abilities with
puzzles are rapidly improving.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.910
In short, you need one as well.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.290
You require an Armlet’s assistance.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:48.290
Orpheus, promise me something.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:54.110
Swear that you will definitely save
Jin if I awaken as a Phi-Brain.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:58.240
What purpose would that serve?

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.700
Just promise me you’ll save him!

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:10.200
Very well. I do not care to linger
in this withering body forever.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:15.560
You have my word.
Once you have awoken as a Phi-Brain,

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.720
I shall release Jin Makata.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.220
I’ll solve a Philosopher’s Puzzle.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.860
And I’ll prove to you that I can
obtain an Armlet of Orpheus!

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:46.500
H-hey! Orpheus?

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:51.200
Don’t do... it, Raetsel!

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.510
Jin!

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:56.540
Raetsel...

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.500
I’ve missed you, Jin!

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:04.390
Don’t don the Armlet of... Orpheus!

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:09.650
You must not... put it on!

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.900
You are gifted with puzzles!

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:17.820
That’s why... your abilities combined with the Armlet...

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:22.200
could lead your mind down the path of destruction...!

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:27.960
That’s enough! Jin, you’ve fought long enough.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.540
Raetsel...

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.800
I know the truth.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:39.000
When you sealed Orpheus,
you sealed your memories with him.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:45.420
Your body... and your mind have been
fighting Orpheus this whole time!

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:50.780
When I go, I swear I will take him down with me!

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.890
Don’t talk that way!

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:57.890
I promise I will save you!

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:01.080
Don’t! Forget about the Armlet!

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.370
Raetsel, I think of you as...

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.670
Jin!

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.500
Jin!

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.140
I shall give it to you.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.170
You may have what you desire.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:25.550
Do not forget: Jin Makata’s life is
drawing close to an end.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:44.290
This maze exists in a dimension
where gravity is warped.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:02.300
That must be the goal...

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:04.850
There is but one rule.

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:08.510
You are only permitted to walk down
the stairs located in this maze.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.480
You must not go up the stairs!

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.730
If you break that rule...

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.060
Are you ready?

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:30.070
Puzzle time... Start!

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:43.620
Isn’t that... Jin and I?!

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:55.980
Cheers!

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:04.890
Isn’t this yummy, Jin?

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.400
We’re here to celebrate safely solving that puzzle.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:12.480
It’s nice to have a fancy dinner like
this every now and then, isn’t it?

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:17.490
Really? Everything you cook is always so yummy, Jin!

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:21.240
But this is a three-star restaurant...

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.800
A three-star...?

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:27.250
Three stars mean it’s SUPER yummy!

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.760
Then your cooking must get a hundred stars!

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.520
A hundred stars?!

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:38.760
You’re too much, Raetsel!

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.360
But thank you anyway.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.640
Hey, let’s have another cheers!

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.010
Sure!

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:50.290
To Raetsel!

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:52.200
To 100-Star Jin!

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.420
Cheers!

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:59.040
How nostalgic...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.660
I truly enjoyed myself back then.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:07.300
Just being with Jin was a blast!

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:15.590
Raetsel, don’t go near that dangerous
puzzle all by yourself ever again!

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.980
But I wanna help you--

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:18.790
Here.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:21.470
What’s this?

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:25.720
My good luck charm.
I’d like you to keep it from now on.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.370
When I’m challenging a Puzzle of Fools,

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:31.190
please pray for my safety and wait for me.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:37.500
It was shortly after that when Jin...

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.090
Don’t let him go!

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:45.660
Go after Jin!

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:50.870
Stop Jin in his tracks! HURRY!

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:56.810
If you don’t stop him, Jin will fight
Count Pythagoras in the Puzzle of God!

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:10.280
Right then... if only I had stopped Jin!

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:21.490
If I become a Phi-brain, I may be able to
intervene with the past and save Jin!

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:26.010
That’s it! I could undo everything!

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:30.720
Hang in there, Jin!

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:36.280
It’s no use, Jin Makata.

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:42.980
Struggle all you may, but your
voice will never reach Raetsel.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:54.790
The Puzzle of God will be ready before much longer.

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:55.840
Indeed?

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:58.070
Excuse me,

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:02.510
but when will I be reunited with Lovushka?

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.070
Soon now.

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:10.340
You had best prepare to embrace
that woman in your arms.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.500
L-Lovushka...!

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:39.920
When we’re out here like this, I can’t help
but get the feeling that it’s all a dream.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:43.000
The hopeless future...

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.550
The way Jin turned into Orpheus...

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:52.270
How Kaito and Freecell are desperately
working to solve the Trial of Puzzles...

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:57.350
Jin is important to him...

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:01.690
I get that, but...

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:12.200
Encountering a puzzle means encountering a person.

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:18.390
Solve them. Set them free, those puzzles.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:21.080
The puzzles have done nothing wrong.

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:24.120
The blame should fall on those who made them.

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:31.130
Jin, he--Orpheus--isn’t a person. He’s a monster!

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:34.660
It’s a hero’s duty to defeat the monster!

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:41.060
Jin...

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:46.650
If only I could see where
Orpheus’ plans are headed...

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.750
Then I could save Jin.

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:53.240
Just now, you were thinking to yourself,

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:55.430
“If I became a Phi-Brain,” weren’t you?

00:13:56.570 --> 00:14:01.690
For you to correctly read my thoughts,
I’m a failure as the director.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:05.880
Could we serve as the trump card
that allows Jin Makata’s mind

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:09.300
to escape Orpheus and this current predicament?

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:16.710
There is no evidence to prove that Jin
actually exists inside of Orpheus.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:22.930
I see... Indeed, Orpheus is the only
one who has made the claim

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:26.720
that “Jin Makata’s mind coexists with Orpheus.”

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:29.210
“I hope that Jin is alive.”

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.820
Orpheus is exploiting the human weakness

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:35.500
in our hearts that ushers such thoughts...

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:43.060
Master Rook?

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:51.000
All four staircases go up?

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.590
There’s no way I can proceed...

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.520
What would it take to get over there?

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:02.600
I have to release this puzzle and
obtain an Armlet of Orpheus...!

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:10.230
I wonder if this is the right way...

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:11.360
Really?

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:14.240
Won’t it lead to another dead end?

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:17.020
Jin!

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.780
That can’t be right, Rook!

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:23.190
You’re the one who’s wrong, Kaito!

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:25.960
I’m sure you’re supposed to take it over here.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:28.750
Kaito Daimon and Rook...

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.620
What’s this supposed to be?

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.380
Huh? It didn’t work!

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:36.170
I told you so!

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:40.300
Go here and then... Huh? What gives?

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:43.540
See! You’re not any better.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:45.310
What was that?!

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:47.230
But it’s the truth!

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:50.150
You two gave it a nice try!

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:51.800
Keep that enthusiasm up!

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:54.850
All righty! I’m gonna solve this puzzle!

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:57.810
Jin... Why do your eyes seem so
kind when you gaze upon Kaito?

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:00.070
I’m going to solve it!

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:01.160
No, I am!

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.780
Now, now! No fighting allowed!

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:07.820
Really! Rook and Kaito are totally helpless.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:13.700
If you two are going to fight over the puzzle,
I’ll solve it for you!

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:18.300
Let’s see... This goes like this...

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:21.840
Wow! You’re amazing, Raetsel!

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:24.710
Good luck, Raetsel! Keep it up!

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:27.810
Just leave this to me!

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:33.740
Raetsel was together with us...

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:36.320
You can do it, Raetsel!

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:44.230
Is this... Is this one of those illusions
Orpheus creates depicting the past?

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:48.620
Oh, Raetsel! Is it supposed to go down here?

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:52.140
It does! You’re amazing, Kaito!

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:53.090
Poopy!

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:58.240
I see a spot! It goes like this over here!

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.000
Rook, you’re also amazing! Incredible!

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:04.750
But I’d still be stuck if you didn’t figure
that one part out, Raetsel!

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:08.560
Rook’s right! You’re awesome, Raetsel!

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:14.940
She can be so cute when she laughs...

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:21.030
If I became a Phi-Brain, I could change the past.

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:25.270
Is Orpheus trying to show that to me?

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:29.910
No, this isn’t Orpheus’ doing!

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:33.650
We did it!

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:36.500
Jin, lookie! Lookie! We solved it!

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:38.370
Aren’t we incredible?

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:41.080
We couldn’t have solved it without Raetsel, right?

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.550
Uh, that’s right...

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:43.660
That’s not true!

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.650
We solved it because all three of us worked together!

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:48.670
Raetsel, you sure are nice!

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:57.930
Only because I love Kaito, Rook and Jin
so very, very, very much!

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.960
Kaito, Rook and Raetsel...

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:08.530
I want all three of you to remember
what has happened here today.

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:12.320
Don't give up what is dear.

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:14.170
Never.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:16.320
Never lose sight of what matters.

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:38.470
I wanted... I wanted to be with them back then...

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:45.850
I wish I could have solved puzzles with
the three of them back then...

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:57.740
Was that a dream? No...

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:04.630
What is the matter, Master Rook?

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:11.060
Master Rook?

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:13.540
There is going to be a change of plans.

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:18.540
Kaito, it looks like you were right.

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:23.520
I will play my role accordingly.

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:27.140
Isn’t that what you’d want, Jin?

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:39.250
In order to move forward, I must take one
of the staircases that climb upwards.

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:41.950
And the correct staircase is...

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.180
I guessed it!

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:04.800
Orpheus created this world.

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:09.570
This is the only staircase where the
gravity works differently.

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:24.800
Jin...

00:21:26.980 --> 00:21:29.220
I’m sorry, Raetsel...!

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:34.930
It’s my fault that you’re going through this...

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.270
It’s okay, Jin.

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:45.070
You showed that to me, didn’t you? Thank you.

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:50.920
I don’t need anything else if that blissful
past could become the present!

00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:54.960
Stop it, Raetsel! You don’t have to
resort to such lengths to find...

00:21:58.140 --> 00:21:59.350
Continue as you are.

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:06.610
Use that Armlet to make your desires become reality!

00:22:08.860 --> 00:22:13.970
Next time, make it a higher-level puzzle, Orpheus.

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:22.330
Don’t be sad, Jin. This is what I want.

00:22:23.290 --> 00:22:26.580
I’ve decided that I’m going to protect you.

00:24:01.930 --> 00:24:06.210
Up? Down? I don’t know!

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:09.520
Think carefully. This is a silly question.

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:10.850
It’s silly...?

00:24:11.730 --> 00:24:12.400
They go up!

00:24:12.400 --> 00:24:13.260
Correct!

00:24:14.610 --> 00:24:15.820
That was easy.

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:17.680
Now we can both get some airtime.

00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:20.240
So you’re also getting some airtime?

00:24:20.240 --> 00:24:23.060
Next time, “Kaito, You’ve Lost.”

00:24:21.030 --> 00:24:27.980
Kaito, You’ve Lost

00:24:23.060 --> 00:24:25.200
I said that I really wanted to make an
appearance without taking some quiz.

00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:26.790
That isn’t fair!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin
Art: Akeru Otsuki
